Relying on paragraph 11 of such decision, learned counsel appearing for the petitioner contends that it is well settled principle of law that the High Court, in exercise of its inherent power, may consider it appropriate to grant exemption from surrendering having regard to the nature and circumstances of a particular case;
and, in view thereof, the High Court was in error in holding that in no case is an application seeking Daulat Singh vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 30 July, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/45725008/
2 exemption from surrendering is maintainable.

